LIB_LOAD("je",{"je1":{"challenge":[{"q":"Where was Jonathan Edwards born?","o":["Connecticut, in America","England","Nigeria","Scotland"],"why":"In 1703."},{"q":"What did young Jonathan study in the woods?","o":["Flying spiders","Lions","Birds' nests","Rivers"],"why":"God's world is full of wonders."},{"q":"What word did Edwards put at the start of each promise?","o":["Resolved","Maybe","Hopefully","Someday"],"why":"It means 'firmly decided'."},{"q":"How many resolutions did he write?","o":["Seventy","Ten","One hundred","Twelve"],"why":"Over a year or so."},{"q":"Resolution 6: \"To live with all my...\"","o":["might","money","friends","sleep"],"why":"While I do live."},{"q":"Who 'purposed in his heart' in Babylon?","o":["Daniel","Jonah","Moses","Peter"],"why":"Daniel 1:8."},{"q":"What did Edwards say he couldn't do without?","o":["God's help","Money","Spiders","Fame"],"why":"He wrote it at the top of his list."},{"q":"\"Without me ye can do...\"","o":["nothing","everything","something","a little"],"why":"John 15:5."},{"q":"How often did Edwards read his resolutions?","o":["Weekly","Yearly","Never","Hourly"],"why":"Once a week."},{"q":"James 1:22 says be doers of the word, and not...?","o":["hearers only","readers","singers","writers"],"why":"Don't forget the mirror!"}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! According to Psalm 111:2, who seeks out the works of the LORD?","o":["All who have pleasure in them","Only kings","Only teachers","Nobody"],"why":"Curiosity is a gift!"},"choices":[{"title":"Decide in advance","q":"You know some friends will offer you a cigarette at the weekend.","o":[{"t":"Decide now what you'll say, and pray about it before you go.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Daniel, purpose in your heart before the test comes."},{"t":"Decide when it happens.","f":"It's much harder to decide in the heat of the moment."},{"t":"Just avoid thinking about it.","f":"Preparation beats panic."}]},{"title":"Trying alone","q":"You keep failing to stop being rude to your sister, however hard you try.","o":[{"t":"Ask God every morning to help you, and keep trying.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Without Him we can do nothing; with Him we bear fruit."},{"t":"Give up. It's just who you are.","f":"God can change you."},{"t":"Try even harder alone.","f":"A branch grows fruit by staying on the vine."}]},{"title":"Forgotten promises","q":"You made great New Year's resolutions, but it's March and you can't remember them.","o":[{"t":"Write them down again and set a weekly reminder to read them.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Edwards read his every week."},{"t":"Forget it until next January.","f":"Every week is a fresh start."},{"t":"Decide resolutions don't work.","f":"They work when you look at them!"}]},{"title":"Curious about creation","q":"Your science teacher says faith and science can't go together.","o":[{"t":"Respectfully share that many believers, like Edwards, loved studying God's world.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! The works of the LORD are great, sought out by those who delight in them."},{"t":"Stop studying science.","f":"Curiosity about creation honours the Creator."},{"t":"Argue loudly in class.","f":"Be respectful and kind."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"newengland","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 of Resolutions in real life."},{"sc":"woods","n":"🕷️ Be curious about God's world. It's full of wonders."},{"sc":"palace","n":"✍️ Decide in advance, like Daniel and Edwards."},{"sc":"vineyard","n":"🍇 Keep your promises with God's help, staying close to Jesus."},{"sc":"home","n":"🪞 Read your resolutions every week, and do them."}],"stops":{"je1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"newengland","n":"In 1703, in a little town in Connecticut, in America, a baby boy was born to a pastor and his wife. His name was {Jonathan Edwards}."},{"sc":"newengland","n":"Jonathan grew up with ten sisters! He was the only boy among eleven children. His father taught him at home, and he learned Latin, Greek and Hebrew."},{"sc":"woods","n":"He was wildly curious. As a boy, he lay in the woods watching spiders float through the air on their silk threads. He wrote a careful essay about how they did it."},{"sc":"woods","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"The spiders let out a thread of silk, and the breeze lifts them up, and away they sail! God's world is full of wonders, if you only look."},{"sc":"college","n":"At about thirteen, he went to college at {Yale}. He read everything he could find: science, thinking, and above all the Bible."},{"sc":"college","w":"jeamaka","e":"shock","t":"College at thirteen? I'm thirteen! I can barely finish my homework."},{"sc":"college","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Ha! Being clever wasn't the most important thing, Amaka. The most important thing happened when I began to see how beautiful God is. Everything looked different after that: the sky, the clouds, the grass. I saw God's glory everywhere."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"Then, as a young man of about nineteen, Jonathan did something unusual. He took a pen and began to write down promises to himself about how he would live."}],"quote":{"text":"The works of the LORD are great, sought out of all them that have pleasure therein.","who":"Psalm 111:2","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"A curious mind, a God-filled heart","text":"Jonathan loved studying God's world, even spiders! But what changed him most wasn't his brains. It was seeing how beautiful God is. Curiosity and faith belong together."},"think":"What part of God's world makes you curious? What could you learn about God by studying it?","quiz":[{"q":"How many sisters did Jonathan Edwards have?","o":["Ten","None","Two","Five"],"why":"He was the only boy among eleven children."},{"q":"What creature did young Jonathan study and write about?","o":["Spiders","Lions","Fish","Horses"],"why":"How they float on silk threads."},{"q":"At about what age did he go to Yale?","o":["Thirteen","Twenty-five","Seven","Forty"],"why":"Very young!"},{"q":"What did he say was the most important thing?","o":["Seeing how beautiful God is","Being clever","Being rich","Being famous"],"why":"Then he saw God's glory everywhere."},{"q":"What did he start writing at about nineteen?","o":["Promises to himself about how he would live","A novel","Songs","A newspaper"],"why":"His resolutions."}]},"je1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"In 1722, Jonathan was a young preacher at a small church in New York. In the evenings, he sat at his desk by candlelight and wrote."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"{Resolved}, to live with all my might, while I do live."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"One by one, he wrote them down. He called them {resolution}s: firm decisions about how he would think, speak, act and use his time. Over the next year or so, the list grew to seventy."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"jekunle","e":"smirk","t":"Seventy? I make one New Year's resolution, and I forget it by the second week of January!"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"I know the feeling, Kunle. But these weren't wishes. They were decisions. I wanted my whole life, every hour of it, to count for God."},{"sc":"palace","n":"Long before Edwards, another young man made a resolution. Daniel was taken as a captive to Babylon as a youth. The king offered him rich food that God's law forbade."},{"sc":"palace","n":"But the Bible says: 'Daniel purposed in his heart that he would not defile himself.' He decided in advance. And when the test came, he was ready."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"That's the power of a resolution. You decide before the moment comes, so you don't have to decide in the heat of it."}],"quote":{"text":"Resolved, to live with all my might, while I do live.","who":"Resolution 6","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Decide before the test","text":"Edwards wrote seventy resolutions: not wishes, but firm decisions. Like Daniel, who 'purposed in his heart' before the test came, a resolution helps you decide in advance, so you're ready when the moment arrives."},"think":"What's one thing you could decide now, before the moment of temptation comes?","quiz":[{"q":"Where was Edwards preaching in 1722?","o":["A small church in New York","London","Lagos","Rome"],"why":"A young preacher."},{"q":"How many resolutions did he write in the end?","o":["Seventy","Seven","Three","Seven hundred"],"why":"Over a year or so."},{"q":"What's the difference between a wish and a resolution?","o":["A resolution is a firm decision","There's no difference","A wish is stronger","A resolution is a joke"],"why":"Edwards made decisions."},{"q":"What did Daniel do in Babylon?","o":["Purposed in his heart not to defile himself","Ate everything","Ran away","Became a soldier"],"why":"Daniel 1:8."},{"q":"Why is it good to decide in advance?","o":["So you're ready when the test comes","So you can forget","It isn't good","To impress people"],"why":"Decide before the moment."}]},"je1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"jeamaka","e":"worried","t":"But seventy promises... Didn't he break them? I'd break them all in a week!"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Of course I broke them sometimes. That's why, at the very top of my list, before even one resolution, I wrote this:"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"Being sensible that I am unable to do any thing without God's help, I do humbly entreat him by his grace to enable me to keep these Resolutions."},{"sc":"vineyard","n":"Edwards knew what Jesus taught His disciples on the night before He died."},{"sc":"vineyard","w":"jejesus","e":"smile","t":"I am the vine, ye are the branches: He that abideth in me, and I in him, the same bringeth forth much fruit: for without me ye can do nothing."},{"sc":"vineyard","w":"jekunle","e":"smile","t":"So a branch doesn't grow grapes by trying really hard. It grows them by staying connected to the vine!"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Exactly. My resolutions weren't a way to make God love me. He already did. They were my way of saying: Lord, this is how I want to live for You. Please help me do it."}],"quote":{"text":"Being sensible that I am unable to do any thing without God's help, I do humbly entreat him by his grace to enable me to keep these Resolutions, so far as they are agreeable to his will, for Christ's sake.","who":"The opening of the Resolutions","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Promises with God's help","text":"Edwards began his list by admitting he couldn't keep a single resolution without God's help. Like a branch on a vine, we bear fruit by staying close to Jesus, not by trying harder alone."},"think":"Is there something good you've been trying to do in your own strength? How could you ask God for help with it today?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Edwards write at the top of his list?","o":["That he couldn't keep them without God's help","A shopping list","His name only","A joke"],"why":"He asked God for grace."},{"q":"Did Edwards ever break his resolutions?","o":["Yes, sometimes","Never","He forgot them all","He tore them up"],"why":"That's why he needed God's help."},{"q":"What did Jesus say He is?","o":["The vine","The branch","The farmer only","The grape"],"why":"Ye are the branches."},{"q":"How does a branch grow grapes?","o":["By staying connected to the vine","By trying very hard alone","By falling off","By shouting"],"why":"Abide in Him."},{"q":"Why did Edwards write resolutions?","o":["To live for God, not to earn His love","To earn God's love","To show off","Because he was bored"],"why":"God already loved him."}]},"je1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"Amaka decided to write her own resolutions. She wrote five, pinned them on her wall, and felt great."},{"sc":"home","n":"Three weeks later, she noticed the paper had fallen behind her desk. She hadn't looked at it once. She'd forgotten every single resolution."},{"sc":"home","w":"jeamaka","e":"worried","t":"Oh no. What was number three again?"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"That's why I wrote one more line at the top of my list: 'Remember to read over these Resolutions once a week.' A promise you never look at is a promise you'll soon forget."},{"sc":"home","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"The Bible says it's like a man who looks at his face in a mirror, then walks away and forgets what he looks like. Don't just hear. Do!"},{"sc":"home","w":"jekunle","e":"big","t":"I know! Put a reminder on your phone, every Sunday evening: 'Read your resolutions.'"},{"sc":"home","w":"jeamaka","e":"smile","t":"And I'll stick them inside my Bible, so I see them every time I read."},{"sc":"home","n":"Every Sunday after that, Amaka read her five resolutions and asked God to help her keep them. Slowly, they stopped being words on paper and became part of who she was."}],"quote":{"text":"Remember to read over these Resolutions once a week.","who":"A note at the top of the Resolutions","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Look in the mirror weekly","text":"A promise you never look at is soon forgotten. Edwards read his resolutions every week. Keep yours where you'll see them, read them often, and ask God to help you do them, not just hear them."},"think":"Where could you keep your own resolutions so that you see them every week?","quiz":[{"q":"What happened to Amaka's first resolutions?","o":["The paper fell behind her desk and she forgot them","She kept them perfectly","She lost her Bible","Kunle stole them"],"why":"She never looked at them."},{"q":"How often did Edwards read his resolutions?","o":["Once a week","Once a year","Never","Once in his life"],"why":"He wrote a reminder at the top."},{"q":"What does James compare a forgetful hearer to?","o":["Someone who looks in a mirror and forgets their face","A tree","A bird","A ship"],"why":"Don't just hear. Do!"},{"q":"Where did Amaka decide to keep her resolutions?","o":["Inside her Bible","In the bin","Under her bed","At school"],"why":"So she'd see them every time she read."},{"q":"What does James 1:22 say to be?","o":["Doers of the word, not hearers only","Hearers only","Writers only","Quiet"],"why":"Put it into action."}]}}},"je2":{"challenge":[{"q":"Resolution 5: never to lose one moment of...","o":["time","sleep","money","food"],"why":"Improve it the best way possible."},{"q":"How did Kunle change his Saturday?","o":["He made a simple plan and chose his time","He slept more","He stayed in bed","He scrolled longer"],"why":"Same 24 hours, felt twice as long."},{"q":"Ephesians 5:16 says: redeeming the...","o":["time","money","house","field"],"why":"Because the days are evil."},{"q":"Resolution 6: to live with all my...","o":["might","heart","friends","toys"],"why":"While I do live."},{"q":"What job did Amaka do half-heartedly?","o":["Sweeping the classroom","Cooking","Washing a car","Reading"],"why":"She hid the dust!"},{"q":"Colossians 3:23 says do it heartily, as to...?","o":["the Lord","your teacher","your friends","yourself"],"why":"And not unto men."},{"q":"Resolution 7 is the test of the last...","o":["hour of my life","day of school","page of a book","bus home"],"why":"See things clearly."},{"q":"1 John 2:28 says abide in Him so we're not...","o":["ashamed at His coming","tired","hungry","late"],"why":"Have confidence."},{"q":"Who did Amaka and Kunle visit for wisdom?","o":["Grandma Ngozi","Coach Bayo","Dayo","Bishop Ryle"],"why":"Eighty-two years of wisdom."},{"q":"\"Teach us to number our...\"","o":["days","coins","sheep","friends"],"why":"Psalm 90:12."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! According to the Yoruba proverb, what can a child not see even from up a tree?","o":["What an elder sees sitting down","The sky","The market","A bird"],"why":"Learn from older people's wisdom."},"choices":[{"title":"Lost Saturday","q":"It's the holidays and you're spending whole days scrolling without noticing.","o":[{"t":"Make a simple daily plan that includes rest, work and time with people.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Choose your hours; don't let them drift."},{"t":"Keep drifting. It's the holidays.","f":"Rest is good, but drifting isn't rest."},{"t":"Fill every second with work and never rest.","f":"Rest is a good use of time too."}]},{"title":"Boring chore","q":"You're asked to tidy the church hall after a programme. Nobody will check.","o":[{"t":"Do it properly, as if for Jesus.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord."},{"t":"Do half and leave.","f":"Live with all your might, not half."},{"t":"Pretend you didn't hear.","f":"Faithful in little, trusted with much."}]},{"title":"The last hour test","q":"You're about to send an angry, hurtful message to someone.","o":[{"t":"Ask: would I be ashamed of this if Jesus came this hour? Then don't send it.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! The last hour test helps you see clearly."},{"t":"Send it. They deserve it.","f":"Would you want that to be your last message?"},{"t":"Send it, then delete it later.","f":"Words can't really be deleted."}]},{"title":"Grandpa's stories","q":"Your grandfather wants to tell you about his life, but you'd rather be on your phone.","o":[{"t":"Put the phone away and listen. Ask what he'd do differently.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Borrow the wisdom of the old."},{"t":"Nod while scrolling.","f":"He'll notice. Give him your full attention."},{"t":"Say you're busy.","f":"What an elder sees sitting, a child can't see up a tree."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"home","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 of Resolutions in real life."},{"sc":"home","n":"⏳ Choose your hours. Don't let them drift away."},{"sc":"college","n":"🔥 Do every job with all your might, as to the Lord."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"🕰️ Use the last hour test to see clearly."},{"sc":"home","n":"👵 Borrow wisdom from older people, and live it now."}],"stops":{"je2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"It was Saturday. Kunle woke up at 10. He scrolled until 11. He watched videos until 1. He napped until 3. By evening, he couldn't remember anything he'd done."},{"sc":"home","w":"jekunle","e":"worried","t":"Where did the whole day go?"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Ah, Kunle. Time is a strange thing. You can't save it in a bank. You can't buy it back. Once a moment is gone, it's gone forever."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"That's why my fifth resolution said: never to lose one moment of time, but {improve} it the most profitable way I possibly can."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"jekunle","e":"shock","t":"Not one moment? So no rest? No fun?"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"No, no! Rest is a good use of time. Fun with friends and family is a good use of time. God made the Sabbath! The problem isn't rest. It's drifting, letting hours slip away without even choosing them."},{"sc":"home","n":"The next Saturday, Kunle made a simple plan: help at home in the morning, football with friends, an hour of reading, and time with his family in the evening. He rested too. But this time, he chose it."},{"sc":"home","w":"jekunle","e":"big","t":"Same 24 hours. But it felt twice as long!"}],"quote":{"text":"Resolved, never to lose one moment of time; but improve it the most profitable way I possibly can.","who":"Resolution 5","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Choose your hours","text":"Time can't be saved or bought back. Edwards resolved never to waste a moment. That doesn't mean no rest or fun; those are good uses of time. It means choosing your hours instead of letting them drift away."},"think":"Where do your hours tend to 'drift away'? What's one small plan that could help?","quiz":[{"q":"How did Kunle spend his Saturday at first?","o":["Scrolling, watching videos and napping","Helping at home","Studying","Playing football"],"why":"And he couldn't remember any of it."},{"q":"What was Edwards's fifth resolution about?","o":["Never losing a moment of time","Never eating sweets","Never laughing","Never sleeping"],"why":"Improve it the best way possible."},{"q":"Did Edwards say rest was a waste of time?","o":["No, rest and fun are good uses of time","Yes, always","He never rested","Only on Mondays"],"why":"The problem is drifting."},{"q":"What did 'improve' time mean in Edwards's day?","o":["Use it well","Make clocks faster","Sleep more","Waste it"],"why":"Get the most good out of it."},{"q":"What does Ephesians 5:16 tell us to do?","o":["Redeem the time","Waste the time","Forget the time","Stop the time"],"why":"Make the most of every opportunity."}]},"je2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"college","n":"Amaka had been chosen to sweep the classroom this week. It was boring. Nobody would notice. She swept half the room and hid the dust under a cupboard."},{"sc":"college","w":"jeamaka","e":"smirk","t":"Good enough. It's only sweeping."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Amaka, my sixth resolution was short: to live with all my might, while I do live. Not half my might. All of it."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"And that's not only for the big things, like exams and competitions. It's for sweeping floors too. The Bible says: whatever you do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men."},{"sc":"college","w":"jeamaka","e":"worried","t":"As if I'm sweeping for Jesus?"},{"sc":"college","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"Exactly! When you do small jobs well, for Him, there's no such thing as a boring job. Every task becomes a gift to God."},{"sc":"college","n":"Amaka took the dust out from under the cupboard and swept the whole room properly. Her teacher noticed the next day, and asked her to be class captain."},{"sc":"college","w":"jeamaka","e":"smile","t":"Whoever is faithful in little things..."}],"quote":{"text":"Resolved, to live with all my might, while I do live.","who":"Resolution 6","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"No half-hearted living","text":"Edwards resolved to live with all his might. Amaka learned that even sweeping can be done 'as to the Lord'. When you do small jobs fully, for Jesus, every task becomes a gift to God, and people notice faithfulness."},"think":"What job do you usually do half-heartedly? How could you do it 'as to the Lord' this week?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Amaka do with the dust at first?","o":["Hid it under a cupboard","Threw it outside","Left it in a pile","Gave it to Kunle"],"why":"\"Good enough.\""},{"q":"What was Edwards's sixth resolution?","o":["To live with all my might while I do live","To sleep all day","To get rich","To be famous"],"why":"Not half my might."},{"q":"According to Colossians 3:23, who do we work for?","o":["The Lord","Only our teachers","Only ourselves","Nobody"],"why":"Do it heartily."},{"q":"What did Edwards say every task becomes when done for Jesus?","o":["A gift to God","A waste of time","A punishment","Boring"],"why":"No such thing as a boring job."},{"q":"What happened after Amaka swept properly?","o":["She was asked to be class captain","She got in trouble","Nobody noticed","She was sent home"],"why":"Faithful in little things."}]},"je2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Here's a test I used, from my seventh resolution. Before I did something, I asked: would I be afraid to do this if it were the last hour of my life?"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"jekunle","e":"worried","t":"That sounds a bit... heavy."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"It's not meant to frighten you, Kunle. It's a way of seeing clearly. When you imagine standing before Jesus, small things look small and big things look big."},{"sc":"college","n":"That week, Kunle was tempted to copy a friend's homework. Then he remembered the test."},{"sc":"college","w":"jekunle","e":"worried","t":"If Jesus came back this hour, would I want Him to find me copying? ...No. I wouldn't."},{"sc":"college","n":"He did his own homework. It took longer. But he felt light and free."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"The Bible says: abide in Him, so that when He appears, we may have confidence, and not be ashamed. That's not fear. That's being ready, like a friend waiting for a friend."},{"sc":"college","w":"jeamaka","e":"smile","t":"It works for good things too! If this were my last hour, I'd want to have said 'I love you' to my mum this morning. So I'm going to call her."}],"quote":{"text":"Resolved, never to do any thing, which I should be afraid to do, if it were the last hour of my life.","who":"Resolution 7","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"See things clearly","text":"Edwards's 'last hour' test helps you see clearly: would I be ashamed to be doing this when Jesus comes? It's not about fear. It's about being ready, like a friend waiting for a friend. And it reminds us to do the good things now."},"think":"Use the 'last hour' test on one choice you'll make tomorrow. What does it show you?","quiz":[{"q":"What was the 'last hour' test?","o":["Would I be afraid to do this if it were the last hour of my life?","Can I finish in an hour?","Is it lunchtime yet?","How fast can I run?"],"why":"Resolution 7."},{"q":"Was the test meant to frighten people?","o":["No, to help them see clearly","Yes","Only children","Only adults"],"why":"Small things look small, big things look big."},{"q":"What was Kunle tempted to do?","o":["Copy a friend's homework","Skip lunch","Go swimming","Read a book"],"why":"Then he used the test."},{"q":"What did Amaka decide to do after hearing the test?","o":["Call her mum to say she loved her","Go to sleep","Watch a film","Nothing"],"why":"It works for good things too!"},{"q":"According to 1 John 2:28, why should we abide in Him?","o":["So we have confidence when He appears","So we get rich","So we're popular","So we can rest"],"why":"Not ashamed at His coming."}]},"je2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"Amaka and Kunle visited Grandma Ngozi, who was eighty-two."},{"sc":"home","w":"jeamaka","e":"smile","t":"Grandma, if you could live your life again, what would you do differently?"},{"sc":"home","w":"jegrandma","e":"smile","t":"Ah, my children. I would worry less about what people thought. I would forgive faster. I would spend less time chasing money and more time with my family. And I would have started following Jesus much, much sooner."},{"sc":"home","w":"jegrandma","e":"smile","t":"But I don't regret the times I was kind. I don't regret one single prayer."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"I often heard old people say how they would live if they could live their lives again. So I made a resolution: to live now the way I'll wish I had lived, when I'm old."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"Why wait until you're eighty to learn what Grandma Ngozi knows? You can borrow her wisdom today!"},{"sc":"home","w":"jekunle","e":"smile","t":"Grandma, can you tell us more? I want to learn it now, not at eighty."},{"sc":"home","w":"jegrandma","e":"big","t":"Sit down, sit down. Bring the tea. I have plenty to say!"}],"quote":{"text":"Resolved, that I will live so as I shall wish I had done when I come to die.","who":"Resolution 17","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Borrow wisdom from the old","text":"Grandma Ngozi wished she had worried less, forgiven faster and followed Jesus sooner. Edwards resolved to live now the way he'd wish he had lived when old. Ask older believers what they'd change, and start living that way today."},"think":"Ask an older person you trust: what would you do differently if you were my age? Write down what they say.","proverb":{"text":"Ohun tí àgbà rí lórí ìjókòó, ọmọdé kò lè rí i bó tilẹ̀ gun igi.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"What an elder sees while sitting down, a child cannot see even after climbing a tree. Learn from the wisdom of older people."},"quiz":[{"q":"How old was Grandma Ngozi?","o":["Eighty-two","Forty","Twenty","One hundred"],"why":"Full of wisdom."},{"q":"What did Grandma say she'd do sooner?","o":["Follow Jesus","Buy a car","Move to Lagos","Retire"],"why":"\"Much, much sooner.\""},{"q":"What did she say she didn't regret?","o":["Being kind and praying","Worrying","Chasing money","Holding grudges"],"why":"Not one single prayer."},{"q":"What did Edwards resolve to do?","o":["Live now the way he'd wish he had lived when old","Wait until he was old","Never listen to old people","Never grow old"],"why":"Borrow wisdom early."},{"q":"What does Psalm 90:12 ask God to teach us?","o":["To number our days","To count money","To sleep well","To run fast"],"why":"That we may apply our hearts unto wisdom."}]}}},"je3":{"challenge":[{"q":"Resolution 16: never to speak ___ of anyone.","o":["evil","well","loudly","quickly"],"why":"Except for real good."},{"q":"What did Kunle's mocking come from?","o":["Jealousy","Hunger","Tiredness","Fear"],"why":"Jealousy hides behind unkind words."},{"q":"What does 'verity' mean?","o":["Truth","Victory","Very","Story"],"why":"Resolution 34."},{"q":"What is a half-truth?","o":["True words used to make people believe something false","A short truth","A funny truth","Half a sentence"],"why":"Still a lie."},{"q":"Ephesians 4:25: putting away lying, speak every man...","o":["truth with his neighbour","loudly","softly","quickly"],"why":"We are members one of another."},{"q":"Resolution 14: never to do anything out of...","o":["revenge","kindness","love","duty"],"why":"Break the chain."},{"q":"What did Jesus pray on the cross?","o":["Father, forgive them","Father, punish them","Father, save me now","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 23:34."},{"q":"\"Vengeance is mine; I will repay, saith...\"","o":["the Lord","Kunle","the king","the teacher"],"why":"Romans 12:19."},{"q":"What is benevolence?","o":["Goodwill towards others","Anger","Laziness","Pride"],"why":"Resolution 70."},{"q":"Colossians 4:6 says let your speech be seasoned with...?","o":["salt","sugar","pepper","honey"],"why":"Always with grace."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! According to the Yoruba proverb, what do harsh words bring out?","o":["An arrow from a quiver","Kola nut","A gift","A song"],"why":"Kind words bring kola nut."},"choices":[{"title":"Behind their back","q":"Your friends are laughing about a new student's accent.","o":[{"t":"Don't join in, and say something kind about the new student.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Never speak evil of anyone, except for real good."},{"t":"Laugh along quietly.","f":"Even laughing along tears someone down."},{"t":"Add your own joke.","f":"Build up, don't tear down."}]},{"title":"Clever answer","q":"Your dad asks if you finished your homework. You did half. You could say \"I did my maths\", which is true.","o":[{"t":"Tell him plainly you've only done half.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! The pure and simple verity."},{"t":"Say \"I did my maths\" and let him assume the rest.","f":"That's a half-truth: true words, false message."},{"t":"Change the subject.","f":"Dodging is not the same as truth."}]},{"title":"Get them back","q":"Someone posts an embarrassing picture of you. You have one of them too.","o":[{"t":"Don't post yours. Ask them to remove theirs, and tell an adult if they won't.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Never act out of revenge."},{"t":"Post theirs. Fair is fair.","f":"Revenge keeps the fire spreading."},{"t":"Post something even worse.","f":"That's adding petrol to the fire."}]},{"title":"Hard feedback","q":"Your friend asks what you think of her song. It needs a lot of work.","o":[{"t":"Mention what's good first, then kindly suggest improvements.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Season it with salt."},{"t":"Say \"It's terrible.\"","f":"True words can still taste bitter without kindness."},{"t":"Say it's perfect.","f":"That's not the plain truth."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"college","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 of Resolutions in real life."},{"sc":"college","n":"🙊 Never tear people down. Say something good instead."},{"sc":"home","n":"💎 Tell the plain truth. No clever twisting."},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"🕊️ No revenge. Forgive like Jesus, and leave it to God."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"🧂 Season every word with kindness."}],"stops":{"je3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"college","n":"Chidi had been made class prefect, and some students weren't happy about it."},{"sc":"college","w":"jekunle","e":"smirk","t":"Chidi only got prefect because the teacher likes him. He's such a show-off. And did you see his shoes? Ha!"},{"sc":"college","w":"jeamaka","e":"worried","t":"Kunle..."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"stern","t":"Kunle, my sixteenth resolution was: never to speak evil of anyone, in a way that would bring them dishonour, unless it was truly for some real good."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Sometimes you must speak up about wrong, to protect someone, or to tell a parent or teacher about danger. That's for real good. But mocking Chidi behind his back? That only tears him down."},{"sc":"college","w":"jekunle","e":"worried","t":"I guess I was just jealous."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"That's honest. Jealousy often hides behind unkind words. The cure is to say something good about the person instead, and mean it."},{"sc":"college","w":"jekunle","e":"smile","t":"Actually... Chidi always helps people with maths. He'll be a good prefect."},{"sc":"college","n":"Chidi heard what Kunle said. The next week, he asked Kunle to help organise the class football team."}],"quote":{"text":"Resolved, never to speak evil of anyone, so that it shall tend to his dishonor, more or less, upon no account except for some real good.","who":"Resolution 16","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Build up, don't tear down","text":"Edwards resolved never to speak evil of anyone, except for real good, like protecting someone from harm. Kunle realised his unkind words came from jealousy. The cure: say something good about the person instead, and mean it."},"think":"Is there someone you often speak badly about? What's one true, good thing you could say about them?","quiz":[{"q":"Why was Kunle mocking Chidi?","o":["He was jealous Chidi became prefect","Chidi was unkind","Chidi stole from him","He was bored"],"why":"Jealousy hides behind unkind words."},{"q":"What was Edwards's sixteenth resolution?","o":["Never to speak evil of anyone, except for real good","Never to speak at all","Always to tease","Never to go to school"],"why":"Don't tear people down."},{"q":"When is it right to speak up about someone's wrong?","o":["For real good, like protecting someone","Never","To make people laugh","When you're jealous"],"why":"Like telling a teacher about danger."},{"q":"What did Kunle say about Chidi in the end?","o":["He always helps people with maths","He's a show-off","He has bad shoes","Nothing"],"why":"Something good, and true."},{"q":"What does James 4:11 say?","o":["Speak not evil one of another","Speak loudly","Speak only to friends","Never speak"],"why":"Build each other up."}]},"je3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"Amaka came home late. She'd been at her friend's house watching a film when she should have been at the library."},{"sc":"home","w":"jeamaka","e":"worried","t":"(I could say I was at the library... and it's only half a lie, because I did walk past it...)"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Amaka, resolution 34: when telling what happened, never to speak anything but the pure and simple {verity}. That means the truth, the whole truth, with no clever twisting."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Half-truths are sneaky. They use true words to tell a lie. 'I walked past the library' is true. But you'd be saying it so your parents believe something false."},{"sc":"home","w":"jeamaka","e":"worried","t":"But I'll get in trouble."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"Maybe a little. But trust is worth more than escaping trouble. Once people know you always tell the plain truth, they'll believe you even when it's hard to believe."},{"sc":"home","w":"jeamaka","e":"worried","t":"Mum, I'm sorry. I wasn't at the library. I was at Ngozi's house watching a film. I should have told you."},{"sc":"home","n":"Her mother was disappointed, and Amaka lost her phone for the weekend. But she also hugged her and said, 'Thank you for telling me the truth.'"}],"quote":{"text":"Resolved, in narrations never to speak any thing but the pure and simple verity.","who":"Resolution 34","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"No clever twisting","text":"Edwards resolved to speak only the plain, simple truth. Half-truths use true words to make people believe something false, and that's still lying. Telling the plain truth may cost a little, but it builds trust that lasts."},"think":"Have you ever told a 'half-truth'? What would telling the plain truth have looked like?","quiz":[{"q":"Where should Amaka have been?","o":["At the library","At school","At church","At the market"],"why":"She was watching a film instead."},{"q":"What does 'verity' mean?","o":["Truth","A lie","A story","A joke"],"why":"An old word for truth."},{"q":"What's wrong with a half-truth?","o":["It uses true words to make people believe something false","Nothing","It's too short","It's too long"],"why":"That's still lying."},{"q":"What did Amaka's mum say?","o":["\"Thank you for telling me the truth\"","\"I don't believe you\"","Nothing","\"Go away\""],"why":"Trust is worth more than escaping trouble."},{"q":"What does Ephesians 4:25 say to put away?","o":["Lying","Books","Friends","Food"],"why":"Speak truth with your neighbour."}]},"je3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"college","n":"Someone had broken Kunle's new pen, on purpose. He found out it was Chidi's little brother, Obi."},{"sc":"college","w":"jekunle","e":"frown","t":"Right. I'm going to break something of his. See how he likes it!"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"stern","t":"Kunle, my fourteenth resolution was very short: never to do anything out of {revenge}."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Revenge feels fair for about one minute. Then the other person wants revenge on you. And on it goes, like a fire that keeps spreading."},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"Jesus showed us another way. When soldiers nailed Him to the cross, mocking Him and gambling for His clothes, He didn't curse them. He prayed."},{"sc":"golgotha","w":"jejesus","e":"worried","t":"Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"That doesn't mean wrong doesn't matter. You can tell a teacher, and Obi should replace the pen. But leave the punishing to God and the people He's put in charge. Don't take it into your own hands."},{"sc":"college","w":"jekunle","e":"worried","t":"Obi, why did you break my pen?"},{"sc":"college","n":"Obi burst into tears. Older boys had dared him to do it. Kunle forgave him, and Chidi made sure Obi saved up his pocket money to buy a new one."}],"quote":{"text":"Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do.","who":"Luke 23:34","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Break the revenge chain","text":"Edwards resolved never to act out of revenge. Revenge keeps the fire spreading. Jesus prayed for the people crucifying Him. Wrong still matters, so tell someone in charge, but leave the punishing to God."},"think":"Is there someone you've wanted to 'get back at'? What could breaking the revenge chain look like?","quiz":[{"q":"What happened to Kunle's pen?","o":["Someone broke it on purpose","He lost it","He sold it","It ran out of ink"],"why":"It was Obi."},{"q":"What was Edwards's fourteenth resolution?","o":["Never to do anything out of revenge","Always get even","Break things back","Ignore everyone"],"why":"Short and strong."},{"q":"What did Jesus pray on the cross?","o":["\"Father, forgive them\"","\"Punish them\"","\"Get them back\"","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 23:34."},{"q":"Why had Obi broken the pen?","o":["Older boys dared him","He hated Kunle","It was an accident","He was hungry"],"why":"He burst into tears."},{"q":"According to Romans 12:19, who says 'Vengeance is mine'?","o":["The Lord","Kunle","The teacher","Obi"],"why":"Leave it to God."}]},"je3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"My very last resolution, number seventy, is one of my favourites. It's just one line: let there be something of {benevolence} in all that I speak."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"jeamaka","e":"worried","t":"In everything? Even when I'm correcting someone? Even when I'm annoyed?"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Especially then! You can say hard things kindly. The Bible says: let your speech be always with grace, seasoned with salt."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"Amaka's mum was cooking egusi soup. Amaka tasted it before the salt went in."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"jeamaka","e":"frown","t":"Mmm... it's a bit flat."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"Her mum added a pinch of salt and stirred. Amaka tasted again."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"jeamaka","e":"big","t":"Wow! Same soup, but now it's delicious!"},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Words are the same. The same message, with a pinch of kindness, goes down well. Without it, even true words taste bitter."},{"sc":"college","n":"The next day, Amaka had to tell her group that their project had mistakes. Instead of 'This is all wrong!', she said: 'We've done great work. Can we fix these three bits together?' Everyone happily agreed."}],"quote":{"text":"Let there be something of benevolence, in all that I speak.","who":"Resolution 70","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Add a pinch of salt","text":"Edwards's last resolution: let there be kindness in everything I say. Like salt in soup, kindness makes even hard words easier to take. You can correct, disagree and say difficult things, all with grace."},"think":"Think of something hard you need to say to someone. How could you 'season it with salt'?","proverb":{"text":"Ọ̀rọ̀ rere ní í yọ obì lápò, ọ̀rọ̀ burúkú ní í yọ ọfà lápó.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"Kind words bring kola nut out of a pocket; harsh words bring an arrow out of a quiver. Kindness opens hearts; harshness starts fights."},"quiz":[{"q":"What is Edwards's last resolution, number seventy?","o":["Let there be benevolence in all I speak","Never speak","Speak loudly","Only speak truth"],"why":"Kindness in every word."},{"q":"What was missing from the egusi soup?","o":["Salt","Pepper","Meat","Water"],"why":"Then it was delicious!"},{"q":"What did Edwards compare kindness in words to?","o":["Salt in soup","Sugar in tea","Water in a pot","Pepper in stew"],"why":"Seasoned with salt."},{"q":"How did Amaka tell her group about mistakes?","o":["Kindly: 'Can we fix these together?'","'This is all wrong!'","She didn't tell them","She shouted"],"why":"Same message, with grace."},{"q":"According to the Yoruba proverb, what do kind words bring out?","o":["Kola nut","An arrow","Money","Tears"],"why":"Harsh words bring out arrows."}]}}},"je4":{"challenge":[{"q":"Resolution 28 is about studying...","o":["the Scriptures","spiders","cricket","money"],"why":"Steadily, constantly, frequently."},{"q":"2 Peter 3:18: grow in...","o":["grace","height","money","fame"],"why":"And in the knowledge of Jesus."},{"q":"When did Edwards do his 'nightly check'?","o":["As he went to bed","At breakfast","At lunch","Never"],"why":"Resolution 37."},{"q":"God's mercies are new every...","o":["morning","year","week","decade"],"why":"Lamentations 3:23."},{"q":"Resolution 56: never give up the fight, however...","o":["unsuccessful I may be","tired I am","late it is","rich I am"],"why":"Keep fighting."},{"q":"\"Fight the good fight of...\"","o":["faith","football","fame","fear"],"why":"1 Timothy 6:12."},{"q":"How many children did Jonathan and Sarah Edwards have?","o":["Eleven","Two","None","Twenty"],"why":"A home full of prayer and music."},{"q":"In which awakening was Edwards a well-known preacher?","o":["The Great Awakening","The Big Sleep","The Long Night","The Morning Bell"],"why":"Many thousands turned to God."},{"q":"In what year did Edwards die?","o":["1758","1703","1900","1650"],"why":"Weeks after becoming president of Princeton."},{"q":"Psalm 119:106: I have sworn, and I will...","o":["perform it","forget it","change it","sell it"],"why":"Keep God's righteous judgments."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Which Hausa proverb means 'Going slowly doesn't stop you arriving'?","o":["Sannu sannu bata hana zuwa","Girman kai rawanin tsiya","Mai haƙuri yakan dafa dutse","None of these"],"why":"Keep going!"},"choices":[{"title":"Bible burst","q":"You read ten chapters of the Bible on Sunday, then nothing all week.","o":[{"t":"Read a little every day instead, with a notebook.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Steadily, constantly, frequently."},{"t":"Keep doing big bursts.","f":"Little and often beats big and rare."},{"t":"Stop reading altogether.","f":"Grow in grace and knowledge."}]},{"title":"Bedtime","q":"You're lying in bed thinking about a mean thing you said today.","o":[{"t":"Tell God, ask forgiveness, and plan to put it right tomorrow.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Search your ways and turn to the Lord."},{"t":"Push it out of your mind.","f":"The replay helps you play better."},{"t":"Lie awake feeling terrible all night.","f":"His mercies are new every morning. Receive them!"}]},{"title":"Failed again","q":"You promised God you'd stop gossiping, and you just did it again.","o":[{"t":"Confess it, get up, and keep fighting.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Never give up the fight, however unsuccessful."},{"t":"Give up. You'll never change.","f":"Losing a battle isn't losing the war."},{"t":"Pretend it doesn't matter.","f":"Fight the good fight of faith."}]},{"title":"Your own list","q":"You want to write your own resolutions but don't know where to start.","o":[{"t":"Pray, then write three that start with 'Resolved', and read them weekly.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Pick up your pen, with God's help."},{"t":"Copy all seventy of Edwards's.","f":"Learn from his, but make yours your own."},{"t":"Wait until New Year.","f":"Today is a fine day to start."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"study","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Resolutions in real life."},{"sc":"study","n":"🌱 Read the Bible steadily, constantly, frequently."},{"sc":"night","n":"🌙 Check your day every night with God."},{"sc":"home","n":"⚔️ Never give up the fight, however many times you fall."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"📜 Write your own resolutions, and read them every week."}],"stops":{"je4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"study","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Resolution 28: to study the Scriptures so steadily, constantly and frequently, that I may find and plainly see myself to grow in knowing them."},{"sc":"study","w":"jekunle","e":"worried","t":"I read the Bible sometimes. But I don't feel like I'm growing."},{"sc":"study","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Look at the words I chose, Kunle: steadily, constantly, frequently. Not one big burst, then nothing for a month. A little, every day."},{"sc":"meadow","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"It's like a plant. You can't see it grow if you stare at it for one minute. But look back after a month, and you'll be amazed."},{"sc":"study","n":"Edwards read his Bible with a pen in his hand. He wrote notes in the margins and filled notebooks with questions and thoughts. He wanted to understand, not just to tick a box."},{"sc":"study","w":"jeamaka","e":"big","t":"I'm going to try that! A notebook for my Bible reading: one thing I learned, one question, and one thing to do."},{"sc":"study","n":"After two months, Amaka flicked back through her notebook. She couldn't believe how much she'd learned."}],"quote":{"text":"Resolved, to study the Scriptures so steadily, constantly and frequently, as that I may find, and plainly perceive myself to grow in the knowledge of the same.","who":"Resolution 28","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Steady, constant, frequent","text":"Edwards resolved to study the Bible steadily, constantly and frequently, so he could see himself grow. Little and often beats big and rare. Try reading with a notebook: one thing learned, one question, one thing to do."},"think":"What would 'steady, constant, frequent' Bible reading look like for you?","quiz":[{"q":"Which three words did Edwards use for how to study Scripture?","o":["Steadily, constantly, frequently","Quickly, loudly, rarely","Once, twice, never","Sadly, slowly, sleepily"],"why":"Resolution 28."},{"q":"What did Edwards compare growth to?","o":["A plant you can't see growing minute by minute","A rocket","A rock","A river"],"why":"Look back after a month."},{"q":"What did Edwards read his Bible with?","o":["A pen in his hand","His eyes closed","Music on","A friend reading for him"],"why":"Notes and questions."},{"q":"What three things did Amaka write in her notebook?","o":["One thing learned, one question, one thing to do","Her shopping list","Jokes","Nothing"],"why":"And she grew!"},{"q":"2 Peter 3:18 says grow in grace and in the knowledge of...?","o":["Our Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ","Mathematics","Spiders","History"],"why":"Grow in Him."}]},"je4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"night","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Here's another habit. Resolution 37: every night, as I go to bed, to ask: where have I been careless? What sin have I committed? Where have I said no to myself for God?"},{"sc":"night","w":"jekunle","e":"worried","t":"Every night? That sounds like a lot of feeling bad."},{"sc":"night","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Not at all! It's like a footballer watching the replay after a match. You don't watch it to feel bad. You watch it to learn, and to play better next time."},{"sc":"night","n":"So Kunle tried it. Lying in bed, he asked God to show him his day."},{"sc":"night","w":"jekunle","e":"worried","t":"Lord, I was rude to my sister at breakfast. I'm sorry. Please help me be kinder tomorrow."},{"sc":"night","w":"jekunle","e":"smile","t":"And thank You for helping me tell the truth to my teacher, even though it was hard."},{"sc":"night","n":"He fell asleep peacefully. The next morning, before anything else, he said sorry to his sister."},{"sc":"night","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"That's it! Search your day, bring it to God, receive His forgiveness, and start fresh in the morning. His mercies are new every morning!"}],"quote":{"text":"It is of the LORD's mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not. They are new every morning: great is thy faithfulness.","who":"Lamentations 3:22-23","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Watch the replay","text":"Edwards checked his day every night, like a footballer watching the replay: not to feel bad, but to learn. Bring your day to God, say sorry, say thank you, and start fresh. His mercies are new every morning."},"think":"Tonight, try Kunle's nightly check: one thing to say sorry for, and one thing to say thank you for.","quiz":[{"q":"When did Edwards check his day?","o":["Every night as he went to bed","Once a year","Never","Only on birthdays"],"why":"Resolution 37."},{"q":"What did Edwards compare the nightly check to?","o":["A footballer watching the replay","A punishment","A test","A party"],"why":"To learn, not to feel bad."},{"q":"What did Kunle say sorry for?","o":["Being rude to his sister","Losing his shoes","Being late","Nothing"],"why":"And he made it right in the morning."},{"q":"What did Kunle say thank you for?","o":["Help to tell the truth","His dinner","Football","Holidays"],"why":"Even though it was hard."},{"q":"What does Lamentations 3:40 tell us to do?","o":["Search and try our ways, and turn to the LORD","Hide our ways","Forget our ways","Run away"],"why":"And His mercies are new every morning."}]},"je4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"home","w":"jeamaka","e":"worried","t":"I keep losing my temper. I've said sorry to God a hundred times. Maybe I'm just an angry person, and I should stop trying."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Amaka, I understand. I wrestled with the same kinds of things. That's why I wrote resolution 56: never to give up, nor in the least to slacken, my fight with my {corruptions}, however unsuccessful I may be."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"jeamaka","e":"shock","t":"'However unsuccessful'? So even you failed again and again?"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"Oh yes. Losing a battle isn't losing the war. The only way to lose for sure is to stop fighting."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"Paul told young Timothy: fight the good fight of faith. Not 'win every round'. Fight! And remember, Jesus has already won the victory. You're fighting on the winning side."},{"sc":"home","n":"Amaka asked her older cousin to pray with her every week about her temper. Slowly, very slowly, she noticed she was snapping less and stopping to breathe more."},{"sc":"home","w":"jeamaka","e":"smile","t":"Not perfect yet. But still fighting!"}],"quote":{"text":"Resolved, never to give over, nor in the least to slacken my fight with my corruptions, however unsuccessful I may be.","who":"Resolution 56","tag":"Edwards's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Losing a battle isn't losing the war","text":"Edwards failed often, but resolved never to stop fighting his sinful habits, 'however unsuccessful'. The only certain way to lose is to give up. Keep fighting, get help from others, and remember Jesus has already won."},"think":"Which battle are you tempted to give up on? Who could you ask to pray with you about it?","proverb":{"text":"Sannu sannu bata hana zuwa.","lang":"Hausa","mean":"Going slowly, slowly doesn't stop you arriving. Keep going, even if progress is slow."},"quiz":[{"q":"What was Amaka struggling with?","o":["Losing her temper","Maths","Football","Sleeping"],"why":"She wanted to give up."},{"q":"What did resolution 56 say?","o":["Never give up the fight, however unsuccessful","Give up when it's hard","Only fight when winning","Never fight"],"why":"Keep fighting."},{"q":"What did Edwards say is the only sure way to lose?","o":["Stop fighting","Lose one battle","Make a mistake","Ask for help"],"why":"Losing a battle isn't losing the war."},{"q":"What did Paul tell Timothy?","o":["Fight the good fight of faith","Give up","Win every round","Run away"],"why":"1 Timothy 6:12."},{"q":"What does the Hausa proverb 'Sannu sannu bata hana zuwa' mean?","o":["Going slowly doesn't stop you arriving","Run fast","Stop now","Never move"],"why":"Slow progress is still progress."}]},"je4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"newengland","n":"So what happened to Jonathan Edwards? He married Sarah Pierpont, a young woman known for her deep love for God. They had eleven children, and their home was full of prayer, music and visitors."},{"sc":"newengland","w":"jesarah","e":"smile","t":"Jonathan studied for long hours, but he always made time for the children. In the evenings, he would sit with us, and we'd talk and pray together."},{"sc":"church","n":"He became pastor of a church in Northampton, Massachusetts. During the {Great Awakening}, many thousands of people in America turned to God, and Edwards became one of its best-known preachers."},{"sc":"church","n":"Later, there were hard times too. His church asked him to leave. He went to the small frontier town of Stockbridge, where he served a community of Native Americans and kept writing books that are still read today."},{"sc":"college","n":"In 1758 he became president of the college now called {Princeton}. Just weeks later, he caught smallpox from an early kind of vaccination, called an inoculation, and died, aged 54. His last words included a message of love for Sarah."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"smile","t":"My life wasn't perfect. But my resolutions helped me aim my whole life at God. Now it's your turn."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"edwards","e":"big","t":"Take a pen. Write three or five resolutions of your own. Start each with 'Resolved'. Begin by asking for God's help. Read them every week. And when you fail, don't give up. Keep fighting!"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"jeamaka","e":"big","t":"Resolved: to be kind to my sister, even when she annoys me."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"jekunle","e":"big","t":"Resolved: to choose my hours, and not let them drift away!"}],"quote":{"text":"I have sworn, and I will perform it, that I will keep thy righteous judgments.","who":"Psalm 119:106","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Pick up your pen","text":"Edwards's life had joy and hardship, but his resolutions kept him aiming at God. Now write your own: three to five, each starting with 'Resolved'. Ask God's help, read them weekly, and when you fail, keep fighting."},"think":"Write your first three resolutions now. Start each one with 'Resolved'. Where will you keep them?","quiz":[{"q":"Who did Jonathan Edwards marry?","o":["Sarah Pierpont","Mary Slessor","Grandma Ngozi","Amaka"],"why":"Known for her deep love for God."},{"q":"What was the Great Awakening?","o":["A time when many thousands turned to God","A very early alarm clock","A war","A storm"],"why":"In the 1730s and 1740s."},{"q":"Where did Edwards go after his church asked him to leave?","o":["Stockbridge, to serve Native Americans","London","Nigeria","Rome"],"why":"And he kept writing."},{"q":"What college did Edwards become president of?","o":["The college now called Princeton","Yale","Oxford","Harvard"],"why":"In 1758."},{"q":"How should you start each of your own resolutions?","o":["With 'Resolved'","With 'Maybe'","With 'Someday'","With 'If I feel like it'"],"why":"Firmly decided, with God's help."}]}}}});
